item.description:
New Features
Open
/config
to search preferences across categories, change supported settings immediately, and see which changes require a restart. (
#52990
,
#53429
)
Send a follow-up while Codex is responding to steer it immediately. Interrupting a turn also stops active Code Mode cells and their nested tool calls. (
#51812
,
#51835
)
Configure a leader key in
/keymap
. The default is
Ctrl+X
, shortcut hints stay open until you choose or cancel, and voice mute moves to
F9
. (
#52273
)
Restart a managed background server from
/daemon
. Codex warns about work the restart could interrupt, then reconnects automatically. (
#53173
)
Codex can run independent read-only tools in parallel, including skill, memory, and conversation-history lookups. (
#52245
)
Daybreak is enabled by default for eligible accounts.
codex exec
can also select it with an OpenAI API key when the server offers access. (
#53701
,
#53717
)
Bug Fixes
Resuming a saved thread restores its permissions and network approvals, while respecting explicit overrides and current managed policy. (
#53150
,
#53419
,
#53424
)
The network proxy now checks permission before a DNS lookup, rejects duplicate
Host
headers, and prevents credential aliases from bypassing inspection hooks. (
#51650
,
#52661
,
#53506
)
Return to an existing side conversation with
/side
after switching threads. Answers to pending prompts also go back to the thread that asked. (
#52184
,
#53436
)
On Windows,
Ctrl+V
and
Shift+Insert
paste text as well as images. On WSL, repeated pastes reuse the clipboard reader, and copy attempts time out instead of hanging. (
#53224
,
#52967
,
#53453
)
Local commands finish promptly when a child keeps an output pipe open. Remote commands preserve late-arriving output so the final poll can still collect it. (
#52652
,
#53331
,
#53622
)
codex exec
no longer prints the same file diff again after an unrelated command. (
#53444
)
Documentation
Updated the bundled OpenAI Docs guidance for migrations to the GPT-6 family, including model-specific reasoning, tool use, and data residency considerations. (
#51768
)
Clarified how the Linux sandbox uses bubblewrap for filesystem isolation and seccomp for syscall filtering. (
#52610
)
Chores
Codex now uses its standard shell executor and no longer bundles a patched
zsh
. Configurations using the retired shell flags receive a migration notice. (
#52160
,
#52213
)
Reduced Linux and macOS release package size by stripping symbols from packaged binaries while preserving them in the original build outputs. (
#52178
)
